WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.534
-Jeremy Allen White.
Jeremy, welcome to the show.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.734
-Thank you.
-Thanks for being here.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:04.767
-Thank you for having me.
-Thank you for coming.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.067
You're not the first
family member

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:09.734
to be
in "The Tonight Show" world.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:11.067
To be at "The Tonight Show."

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.434
-That's right. Yeah.

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.701
I think you always want
your children to outshine you.

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.367
I just didn't know it was gonna
happen this early.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:20.868
My 3-year-old daughter, Ezer,
came here, what,

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.234
like two months ago, six weeks
ago or something like that

00:00:23.234 --> 00:00:25.601
and got to hang out with you.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.567
-Dakota Johnson is
her godmother?

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.567
-Yeah, Dakota's her godmother.

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:34.067
And she's a really big fan of
Angel Moon, which is this...

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:37.801
-Chris Martin.
-Puppet in Coldplay's new album.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.801
-They have like a muppet band
called The Weirdos.

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.133
-The Weirdos. Yeah.
-And they're all muppets.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:44.701
-They're all muppets.
-And they're from space.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.801
-They were on the show.
It wasn't even Chris, really.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.467
-No, they were booked on
the show, yeah.

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.901
And then this beautiful little
baby was walking around

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.534
with Dakota, and she was like,
"Angel Moon, Angel Moon."

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:56.400
She was, like, so cute. And she
was like -- I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.300
Like, no one could stop
looking at this kid.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.767
-Yeah.
-Somebody took a picture of me

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:02.267
doing our exchange,
I want to say.

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:03.801
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Look at that hair.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:06.334
-I did not know
it was your baby.

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:08.267
That's Adam Sandler's
Hawaiian shirt.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.300
-Oh, nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.868
Man, she's met Adam Sandler,
too.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.234
She's really like --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:13.767
-She had a great --
-Really shining, man.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.400
-She's welcome back whenever.
-Cool.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.534
-I'm happy that you're here,
because man, oh, man, did I hear

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.300
more about this show
than anything on Earth.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.701
"The Bear."
-"The Bear."

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.968
-Everyone -- It's almost like --
I don't know if the Internet was

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.501
finding me or thinking that
I would be really into it.

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.200
But everybody's like, "You got
to watch 'The Bear.'

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.200
It's the must-see show."
I'm like, "I get it.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.467
'The Bear.' What is it about?
Is it about a bear?

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.801
What is going on?"

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:36.167
I had no clue what it's about.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:38.601
It's like, no, it's about
a restaurant in Chicago.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:39.934
-Yes.
-I go, "Okay.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:41.601
I still have nothing to do
with Chicago."

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.501
I like food. Fine.
-Yeah, food.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.501
It sounds like you'll like it.
Yeah.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:46.868
-It doesn't. Why?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:48.334
I have no connection.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:49.734
I love it.
-You love it?

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.234
-The Internet was right.
-Oh, good.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.501
-Everyone who told me was right.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:54.100
It's like 100% on
Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.467
-It's doing really well, man.
-You crush it.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.000
How do we explain it
to everyone?

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.100
It's very fast.
I will say, it moves fast.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.868
You could probably binge this
in a weekend.

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.467
-Yeah, yeah.
It's like 4 1/2 hours.

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.200
It's eight episodes.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.501
And I think we were trying to
capture, like, the pace

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.400
of a kitchen, which is
really, really intense.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.300
And the show is about a young
chef, Carmen Berzatto,

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.467
coming home to Chicago
after working in these, like,

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:19.234
really intense kitchen
environments all over the world.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:22.534
And he comes home, and he
kind of inherits his family's

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:26.634
sandwich shop after his brother
passes away.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:29.501
So he comes back, and he's --
he's trying to kind of, like,

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:32.901
bring this shop to
a different sort of glory.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:35.634
And he's also dealing with
the death of his brother.

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.868
-Yeah. People are loving, also,

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.434
the attention to detail
in this show.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.634
And I will say, that right
there -- anyone who -- Yeah.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.434
-That's a deli, is what they
call it, right there.

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.100
-If you drink out of that
plastic deli thing --

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.968
That's what chefs drink out of.
-You're the real deal.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.734
-Did you do your homework
for that?

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:52.367
Like, how did you realize that?
-Yeah.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:54.534
So, we did a lot of work.

00:02:54.534 --> 00:02:57.133
I spent a lot of time
in kitchens.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:59.300
The kitchen I spent the most
time at was a restaurant

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.868
in L.A. called Pasjoli.

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:03.100
It's in Santa Monica.
Chef Dave Beran is chef there.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.234
He's really incredible.
They have a star --

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:06.834
a Michelin star,
which is kind of like

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.100
the biggest deal
in the restaurant world.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.133
-Did people know who you are
at the time,

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.400
before "The Bear" came out?

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.367
-So, we were all in masks.
I was in the kitchen.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:16.634
It's an open kitchen.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:19.734
So it was kind of fine.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:23.100
And I liked that I could be
there, you know.

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.601
Everybody was like,
"This is just some actor."

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:26.801
And they didn't really give it
any thought.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.033
The show hadn't come out.
They didn't know anything

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:29.801
about the show, so I felt very,

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:32.267
like, you know, safe there.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.868
-Yeah.
-But yeah, yeah.

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:36.634
We did all our homework. And we
had these wonderful chefs.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.767
Matty Matheson, who's a really
incredible chef,

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:43.534
Courtney Storer, who's the
showrunner's sister, was a chef

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.834
at this place
Jon &amp; Vinny's in L.A.

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:48.300
So that authenticity that came
from these guys.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.501
-I've had it.
-Yeah, that place is great.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:51.534
-Yeah. So good.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:54.634
-I went to a place called
Mr. Beef,

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:55.868
I want to say, in Chicago.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.400
-Yeah. That's where we shoot.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.133
-I was there. I'm in that place.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:01.033
Is your face up on the wall?
-I think my face is on the wall.

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:02.234
-Your face is probably
on the wall.

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:03.367
-I think I am on the wall.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:04.467
-Oh, I hope I don't take you
out of character

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:05.801
next time you're doing this.
-I know.

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.133
I'm just going to make eye
contact with you as I'm --

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.767
-You're like, "Look, they let
any moron in this place."

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:13.501
You throw a drink at the picture
and have it splash off me.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:15.133
But I'd love to make a cameo.
-Sweet.

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.801
-Yeah. I want to show everyone
a clip of "The Bear."

00:04:17.801 --> 00:04:19.367
Check this out.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.033
-Time to try the new sandwiches.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.133
Behind. Order!

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.968
Marcus, rolls, please, Chef.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.434
[Bleep] Again.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.767
That's crumbly. It's too dense.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:36.267
-Doing it by hand.
-Yo.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:38.000
-It's the mixer.
-It's not the mixer, alright?

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.267
It's crumbly.
The oven's too dry.

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:41.000
You need to fill a baking sheet
with water,

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.834
put it on the oven floor,
throw in another batch, okay?

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:44.534
-Don't tell me how to do my job.
-Just do it.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.434
Yo!
Somebody come try this, cousin.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:51.634
-Yeah, right!

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:54.467
-That was done perfect.
-There you go, Chef.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:56.367
Chef.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:58.100
What's going on?
What do you think?

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:00.467
-It's redundant and white,
just like you.

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:02.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.767
-Redundant and white,
just like -- yes, chef!

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.133
Jeremy Allen White.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.767
Season one of "The Bear" is
streaming right now on Hulu.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.234
We'll be right back with
a performance from Angel Olsen.

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:13.300
Stick around.

